# Paperia PHP Standards

Follow WordPress Coding Standards. Prefer maintainability over short code. Never duplicate logic.

## Security

Always sanitize input:

- `sanitize_text_field()`
- `sanitize_email()`
- `esc_url_raw()`
- `absint()` / `sanitize_key()` when appropriate

Always escape output:

- `esc_html()`
- `esc_attr()`
- `esc_url()`
- `wp_kses_post()`

Never read `$_POST` / `$_GET` / `$_REQUEST` without sanitization. Use nonces for all forms.

## Data access

- Prefer WordPress APIs (`WP_Query`, `get_posts`, options, transients).
- Do not write raw SQL unless absolutely necessary; if required, use `$wpdb->prepare()`.

## Structure

- `functions.php` only bootstraps: define constants, `require_once` modules from `inc/`.
- One responsibility per function.
- Prefix functions/classes/hooks with `paperia_` (or namespaced `Paperia\`).
- Enqueue assets via `wp_enqueue_style` / `wp_enqueue_script` on `wp_enqueue_scripts`.
- Register menus, supports, and image sizes in a dedicated `inc/setup.php`.

## Templates

```php
// ❌ BAD — large markup in page.php
// ✅ GOOD
get_template_part( 'template-parts/content/content', 'page' );
```

Use semantic HTML5 (`header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `article`, `footer`).
